==Mechanics==
[[File:Dizana's quiver - extra ammunition slot.png|frame|The extra ammunition slot above the original slot, only appearing if the quiver is in the inventory or equipped.]]
[[File:Dizana's quiver interface.png|thumb|The quiver's interface when opening it]]
The quiver provides an additional ammunition slot, which can only be filled with [[arrows]] or [[bolts]]. This second ammunition slot allows players to do any of the following:
* Equip two different ammunition types (e.g., bolts and arrows), with the applicable type shot depending on the player's currently equipped ranged weapon (neither [[Javelin|javelins]] nor [[Atlatl dart|atlatl darts]] can be stored in the quiver's ammo pouch).
* Equip two of the same ammunition type (e.g., different types of bolts), with the ammo in the actual ammo slot prioritised (similar functionality to the [[bolt pouch]], but without a left click option to swap ammunition from the [[Worn Equipment]] tab).
* Equip ammunition in the quiver's ammo slot and an item in the original ammo slot, such as a [[god blessing]].

Players can move ammo from their ammo slot into Dizana's quiver using the ''Fill'' option from the Worn Equipment tab. Attempting to do so with no equipped ammo results in the message {{mes|You have nothing in your worn quiver to fill your Dizana's Quiver with.|color=tomato}}{{sic}}

===Charging===
Dizana's quiver outclasses [[Ava's assembler]] in ranged offence in its uncharged state. This can be further increased by charging it with [[sunfire splinter]]s, giving it a passive effect known as ''Dizana's Sunfire''; players can add up to 20,000 charges to the quiver.

When charged, arrows and bolts that are shot from either [[Worn Equipment#Ammunition_slot|ammunition slot]] will gain an additional +1 [[Ranged Strength]] and +10 [[Ranged accuracy]]. As the ammunition must be storable in the quiver, ''Dizana's Sunfire'' will '''not''' apply to other types of ammunition, such as darts shot from a [[toxic blowpipe]], [[chinchompa]]s, or the [[bow of Faerdhinen]].

Whether or not the quiver consumes a charge is determined by a random 1/3 roll.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1842187697978278254|date=4 October 2024|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27963341|archivedate=4 October 2024|quote=[Wondering if you can provide any info about how Dizana's Quiver uses charges. The wiki states we still don't know how it works fully, and that there's some conflictions. I appreciate you, thank you!] It's doing a random 1/3 roll. Hiya :)}} Ranged weapons with a charge system of their own, most notably the [[venator bow]], '''will not''' use the quiver's charges.

Charging the quiver contributes to the required amount of [[sunfire splinters]] required for the [[blessed Dizana's quiver]].

===Exchanging===
Players may exchange the uncharged quiver at [[Minimus]] for 4000 Sunfire Splinters or a 1/200 chance for the Sol Heredit pet. 

