===Upgrading===
After completion of [[Animal Magnetism]] players can bring the quiver to [[Ava]], along with [[Ava's assembler]], [[Ava's accumulator]], or their [[max cape]] equivalents, to apply the same ammunition-saving effect of her devices to the quiver. Doing so will '''not''' consume the devices. Upgrading the quiver with the [[ranging cape]] will only provide the effect of Ava's accumulator; the quiver must be combined with Ava's assembler to receive its effect. This upgrade applies to '''all''' quivers the player owns, now and in the future - if a player loses all of their quivers and obtains a new one, they will '''not''' need to go back to Ava to reobtain the ammo-saving effect. The interaction between Ava devices and metal torsos '''does not''' carry over when adding the Ava effects to the Dizana's quiver.

Players can also use it on a [[Shrine of Ralos]] - whilst having 150,000 [[sunfire splinters]] ({{Coins|-{{GEP|sunfire splinters}}*150000}}) in their inventory - to upgrade it to a [[blessed Dizana's quiver]]. This makes it so that ''Dizana's Sunfire'' is a permanent effect, and allows it to be combined with the [[max cape]] to create [[Dizana's max cape]]. Charging the quiver with sunfire splinters contributes to the required amount of splinters to upgrade.

Due to rounding, the progress towards blessing percentage will only visually increment up every 1,500 splinters used, meaning using less than 1,500 splinters will result in the quiver inaccurately stating its progression is 0%. The quiver going to 0 charges naturally through use does not reset progress towards blessing.
{{bug|Fully uncharging the quiver manually '''will reset all progress towards blessing'''.}}

===Wilderness===
If the player dies below level 20 [[Wilderness]], it will remain in the player's inventory but will be unusable and require {{NoCoins|270000|c}} to repair. If the player is killed by another player, below level 20 Wilderness, {{NoCoins|270000|c}} will be dropped along with any ammo that the quiver was holding, as well as all the charges.

Above level 20 Wilderness, {{NoCoins|9600|c}} will be dropped, along with any ammo in the quiver; the quiver itself and its charges will be destroyed in the process. The quiver - along with its [[Dizana's max cape|max cape variant]] - can be locked by bringing it, along with a [[trouver parchment]] and {{NoCoins|500000|c}}, to [[Perdu]]. This will allow the quiver to be kept upon death to another player above 20 wilderness but any ammo that the quiver was holding, as well as all the charge will be lost.

'''NOTE: Partial charging is lost as well.'''

